# 🧠 Explanation of the Code

# We use two dummy nodes:

# dummy1 for the list of nodes with values less than x.

# dummy2 for the list of nodes with values greater than or equal to x.

# prev1 and prev2 are pointers that build the two separate lists.

# We loop through the original list:

# If current.value < x, we attach it after prev1.

# Otherwise, we attach it after prev2.

# We correctly update both .next and .prev pointers during the attachment.

# After traversal:

# We terminate the greater list by setting prev2.next = None.

# We connect the two lists by linking prev1.next = dummy2.next.

# We update the .prev of the new greater list head back to prev1 if needed.

# Finally:

# The new head of the list is set to dummy1.next.

# And we ensure self.head.prev = None to properly set the head’s .prev.

# This handles all cases:

# Empty list

# All nodes < x

# All nodes >= x

# Mixed lists





